%I A396919 #77 Aug 07 2026 01:05:04
%S A396919 12,18,20,28,44,50,52,68,76,92,98,116,124,148,164,172,188,212,236,242,
%T A396919 244,268,284,292,316,332,338,356,388,404,412,428,436,452,508,524,548,
%U A396919 556,578,596,604,628,652,668,692,716,722,724,764,772,788,796,844,892,908,916,932,956,964,1004
%N A396919 Numbers of the form 4*p or 2*p^2, where p is an odd prime.
%C A396919 The even terms of A054753. The parity-based decomposition of sequence A054753 is structural. Every odd term is of the form p^2*q, where p and q are distinct odd primes (A398421), whereas every even term takes exactly one of two forms: 4*p or 2*p^2.
%C A396919 Together with A398421, this sequence forms a disjoint partition of A054753 into its even and odd terms.
%C A396919 Every term has prime signature [1,2], so A001222(a(n)) = A001221(a(n)) + 1 = 3.
%C A396919 Every term has exactly 6 positive divisors. Equivalently, these are the even terms of A030515 except for {32} = {2^5}.
%C A396919 The sequence is the disjoint union of two even forms: 4*p and 2*p^2.
%C A396919 The relative asymptotic density of this sequence within A054753 is 1/(4*P(2)) = 0.552794751106..., where P(2) = A085548. - _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 01 2026
%F A396919 Equals 4*A065091 disjoint union 2*(A001248 \ {4}).
%F A396919 Equals (A054753 intersection A008586) disjoint union (A054753 intersection A258211).
%F A396919 Equals A054753 \ A398421.
%F A396919 Equals A054753 intersection A005843.
%F A396919 Equals (A030515 intersection A005843) \ {32}.
%e A396919 a(1) = 12 = 2^2*3 is a term of the form 4*p.
%e A396919 a(2) = 18 = 2*3^2 is a term of the form 2*p^2.
%e A396919 20 = 2^2*5 and 44 = 2^2*11 are terms of the form 4*p.
%e A396919 50 = 2*5^2 and 98 = 2*7^2 are terms of the form 2*p^2.
%e A396919 32 = 2^5 is not a term because it has no odd prime factor.
%e A396919 45 = 3^2*5 is not a term because it is odd; it belongs to A398421.
%e A396919 60 = 2^2*3*5 is not a term because A001221(60) = 3 and A001222(60) = 4, whereas the terms must satisfy A001221(n) = 2 and A001222(n) = 3.
%t A396919 seq[lim_] := Union[4*Select[Range[3, lim/4], PrimeQ], 2*Select[Range[3, Sqrt[lim/2]], PrimeQ]^2]; seq[1004] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 01 2026 *)
%o A396919 (Python)
%o A396919 from math import isqrt
%o A396919 from sympy import primepi
%o A396919 from oeis_sequences.OEISsequences import bisection
%o A396919 def A396919(n):
%o A396919     def f(x): return n+x+2-primepi(isqrt(y:=x>>1))-primepi(y>>1)
%o A396919     return bisection(f,n,n) # _Chai Wah Wu_, Aug 06 2026
%Y A396919 Cf. A001221, A001222, A001248, A005843, A014612, A030515, A054753, A065091, A072357, A085548, A095990, A096156, A398421.
